# Pairs with ReclamationEventuallyAdvances. An abandoned call is never retired
# from the registry, whether it lands or not, so it bounds the watermark for
# ever: no reader passes it, no checkpoint advances over it, and the WAL is never
# reclaimed. The base retires the window once its provider call settles.
MODULE: ReclamationEventuallyAdvancesAbandonedCallNeverSettles
TARGET: ReclamationEventuallyAdvances
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: an abandoned call is never retired, so it holds the watermark for ever
PERTURBS: LateLand, SettleHole

--- FIND
    /\ o \in orphans
    /\ orphans' = orphans \ {o}
    /\ durable' = IF o \notin durable /\ o >= tail THEN durable \cup {o} ELSE durable
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a landed call stays in the registry.
    /\ o \in orphans
    /\ orphans' = orphans
    /\ durable' = IF o \notin durable /\ o >= tail THEN durable \cup {o} ELSE durable
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ orphans' = orphans \ {o}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, inflight, durable, tail, acked>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a settled call stays in the registry.
    /\ orphans' = orphans
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, inflight, durable, tail, acked>>
--- END